# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# SECRETS — nothing in this block may ever be committed.
#
# `.env.local` files in this repo hold POG_SIGNER_PRIVATE_KEY, the sole trust
# root of the quota system: whoever holds it can sign an arbitrary allocation
# for an arbitrary address.  The root `.env` holds the deployer PRIVATE_KEY and
# BASESCAN_API_KEY.  The patterns are deliberately broad — a new `.env.staging`
# should be ignored by default rather than by remembering to add it.
#
# Committed templates carry NO values: `.env.example`, `.env.production.example`.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
!.env.production.example

*.key
*.pem
*.keystore

# ─── Dependencies ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
node_modules/

# ─── Foundry build output ────────────────────────────────────────────────────
cache/
out/
foundry.lock

# Broadcast logs: keep real deployment receipts (they are the record of what is
# live on which chain), drop local-anvil and dry-run noise.
/broadcast/*/31337/
/broadcast/**/dry-run/

# ─── Next.js / frontend build output ─────────────────────────────────────────
.next/
build/
.vercel/
next-env.d.ts
*.tsbuildinfo

# ─── Static analysis output ──────────────────────────────────────────────────
# `slither --json` is ~8 MB of AST-derived detail that regenerates in ~15 s and
# goes stale the moment a contract changes. The triage that matters lives in
# docs/SECURITY_AUDIT.md §5.7; reproduce the raw report with the command
# recorded there.
slither.json
slither-run.txt

# ─── Local scratch ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Anvil fork snapshots and one-off scratch files from debugging sessions.
.fork-*.json
.tmp_*
*.log

# The watcher's resume point, harvested hook set and STATE-06 window. Per
# deployment, not per repository: committing one machine's cursor would make
# every other machine rescan or, worse, skip the blocks in between.
monitoring/.watch-state*.json

# ─── OS / editor ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
*.swp
.idea/
.vscode/

scripts/.drill-state.json

# Q1 drill working files: the Safe address and timings are published in
# INCIDENT_RESPONSE.md §8.3 once the run is scored, but the collected
# signatures are other people's and have no business in git.
scripts/.q1-state.json
scripts/.q1-request.json
scripts/.q1-signatures.json

# Real Safe signer addresses + their proof-of-control signatures (PM-D4).
# Template is safe-owners.example.json.
safe-owners.json
